# Local Claude Code config (worktrees, lock files, per-machine overrides).
#
# .claude/settings.json is the ONE exception and is committed deliberately:
# hooks and permissions belong to the project, not to a machine, and this repo
# is developed across two of them (Windows and macOS). Leaving it ignored meant
# every hook and permission had to be re-added by hand on each machine, and
# drift between them was silent — see GitHub issue #193.
#
# settings.local.json stays ignored on purpose. That is where genuinely
# machine-specific overrides go, and user-scope keys that cannot live in
# project settings at all (autoContinueAtUsageLimit) belong in
# ~/.claude/settings.json.
# NOTE the trailing `/*` rather than `/`. Git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so `.claude/` plus a negation silently does
# nothing — the exception has to exclude the directory's contents instead.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
